The ./.wikiignore exclusion subsystem: a single repo-root-anchored matcher (fail-closed on malformed patterns and on parent-exclusion re-include) that all three index passes and the check/discovery surfaces load once and apply identically, so a path excluded on one surface is excluded on every other. Two freshness signals keep it honest: the matcher's contents hash is one of the canonical fingerprint inputs a generation is keyed by, and comparing that hash against the base generation is the sole signal to run the full bidirectional Tree reconciliation, so an un-ignore re-adds paths to --source head/index as well as an ignore removing them.
